abled reports whether v1 checkpoint writes should still\n// happen. checkpoints_v2_only disables the v1 path entirely.\nfunc (s *EntireSettings) IsCheckpointsV1WriteEnabled() bool {\n\treturn !s.IsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled()\n}\n```\n\nIt's a one-liner negation and appears in only a handful of call sites, each of which could just call `!IsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled(ctx)` directly. Adding a whole method + package-level shim + dedicated table-driven test for `!x` is more surface area than it's worth. If you keep it, fine — but the accompanying `TestIsCheckpointsV1WriteEnabled` table is three cases of literally `!s.IsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled()`; consider deleting it, since `TestIsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled_*` already covers the input matrix.\n\nAlso note: the package-level `IsCheckpointsV1WriteEnabled` defaults to `true` when settings can't load, while `IsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled` defaults to `false`. That's the right fail-safe but the package-level doc should say so explicitly — otherwise a future caller could assume the two are perfect inverses.\n\n## 6. Integration tests — large copy-paste\n\n`TestV2Only_FullWorkflow` and `TestV2Push_V2OnlySkipsV1Branch` are essentially copy-paste of the existing dual-write tests, re-verifying what's already verified. The only truly new assertions are:\n\n- v1 metadata does **not** exist (condensation test)\n- v1 branch is **not** pushed to remote (push test)\n\nEverything else (v2 /main exists, /full/current exists, transcript contents) is already covered by `TestV2DualWrite_FullWorkflow` and `TestV2Push_FullCycle`.\n\nTwo options, both fine:\n\n- **Focused deltas**: keep the new tests but trim them to just the v1-absent assertions plus one \"and v2 still works\" smoke. Half the length.\n- **Table-driven**: convert `TestV2DualWrite_FullWorkflow` / `TestV2Push_FullCycle` into subtests keyed on `map[string]any` (strategy_options), with one subtest per mode: `v1-only`, `dual-write`, `v2-only`. Keeps assertions co-located and eliminates three parallel copies of 30-line setup boilerplate.\n\nSame pattern applies to `TestIsCheckpointsV2OnlyCommitted` and `TestPrintCheckpointsV2OnlyMigrationHint` — they re-implement the exact fixture dance of the existing `TestIsCheckpointRemoteCommitted` / `TestPrintSettingsCommitHint`. A small helper (e.g. `commitSettingsFile(t, dir, body)`) would shrink both sets significantly.\n\n## 7. Minor\n\n- `printCheckpointsV2OnlyMigrationHint` uses backtick-quoted CLI strings containing embedded `\"v2\"`. That renders as `entire migrate --checkpoints \"v2\"`, which is correct but unusual-looking. If the CLI flag parser accepts `v2` unquoted (it does for all other `--checkpoints` usage in this repo), drop the quotes for a cleaner hint:\n  ```\n  Run 'entire migrate --checkpoints v2' to migrate existing checkpoints to v2.\n  Use 'entire migrate --checkpoints v2 --force' to rewrite all checkpoints in v2.\n  ```\n- `TestPrintCheckpointsV2OnlyMigrationHint`'s \"prints only once per process\" subtest asserts `count == 2`, because each invocation prints **two** lines containing the substring `entire migrate --checkpoints \"v2\"`. That's correct but non-obvious. Either count a more specific substring (e.g., `--force`) and assert `== 1`, or add a code comment — otherwise the next reader will think the assertion is wrong.\n- `checkpoint_remote.go` block that's now gated on `IsCheckpointsV1WriteEnabled`: its comment still reads \"If the checkpoint branch doesn't exist locally, try to fetch it from the URL.\" Clarify that this is the v1 metadata branch specifically — otherwise the gating looks unrelated to its body.\n\n## Summary of suggested diffs\n\n- Collapse the attach v2-only branching into one linear flow (saves a `settings.Load` and a branch).\n- Hoist the `writeTaskMetadataV2IfEnabled` call out of the `v2Only`/`else` branches in `CondenseSession`.\n- Replace the v2 linear-scan for `sessionID` with a `V2GitStore.ReadSessionContentByID` helper mirroring v1.\n- Rewrite the dynamic-`label` block in `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` as two explicit branches.\n- Either delete `TestIsCheckpointsV1WriteEnabled` or trim it to one smoke case, since it's `!IsCheckpointsV2OnlyEnabled`.\n- Trim `TestV2Only_FullWorkflow` and `TestV2Push_V2OnlySkipsV1Branch` to only assert the v1-absent deltas, or fold all three modes into a subtest table.\n- Drop the `condense_skip_test.go` `ENTIRE_TEST_TTY` hunks from this PR if they belong to the unrelated merge.\n\nNothing is a correctness problem — the main themes are just \"flatten the branches, don't re-test things, and keep the v2 store API symmetrical with v1.\"\n\n I'm noticing that V2GitStore lacks a `ReadSessionContentByID` method, so the v2Only branch has to do a linear search through `summary.Sessions` instead. To improve this, we'd want to add that method to V2GitStore. Now I'm putting together concrete, actionable feedback for the review."}]}}
